    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Detect music beat positions in a local audio or video file. Video inputs are\r\ndecoded to a temporary audio track in the runner.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --input TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Input audio or video file path.\r\n          --output TEXT       Optional: write the full beats_json result to this path.\r\n          --mode <beats|melody> \r\n                              Detection mode: beats (default) or melody.\r\n          --level INT:INT in [0 - 4] \r\n                              5-gear level (0..4). Default 4 for level-count=5, 1 for\r\n                              level-count=2.\r\n          --level-count INT:{2,5} [5]  \r\n                              Beat level scheme: 5 (default) for 5-gear, 2 for 2-gear.\r\n          --upload-vid TEXT   Optional: skip upload and reuse an existing TOS vid.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli media beats --input /tmp/song.m4a\r\n  $ lyra-cli media beats --input /tmp/clip.mp4 --output /tmp/beats.json --level 3\r\n  $ lyra-cli media beats --input /tmp/song.m4a --level-count 2\r\n  $ lyra-cli media beats --input /tmp/song.m4a --upload-vid v0123abcd\r\n\r\nNOTES\r\n  - Audio inputs (m4a/mp3/wav/...) are uploaded as-is.\r\n  - Video inputs are demuxed to a temporary m4a inside the runner; the\r\n    temporary file is removed when the request finishes.\r\n  - --upload-vid skips upload and uses an existing TOS vid.\r\n  - --level applies to the 5-gear API only (0=Level1Half, 1=Level1, ...).\r\n  - --output writes the full beats_json envelope to disk.\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "Detect music beat positions in a local audio or video file. Video inputs are\r\ndecoded to a temporary audio track in the runner.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --input TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Input audio or video file path.\r\n          --output TEXT       Optional: write the full beats_json result to this path.\r\n          --mode <beats|melody> \r\n                              Detection mode: beats (default) or melody.\r\n          --level INT:INT in [0 - 4] \r\n                              5-gear level (0..4). Default 4 for level-count=5, 1 for\r\n                              level-count=2.\r\n          --level-count INT:{2,5} [5]  \r\n                              Beat level scheme: 5 (default) for 5-gear, 2 for 2-gear.\r\n          --upload-vid TEXT   Optional: skip upload and reuse an existing TOS vid.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli media beats --input /tmp/song.m4a\r\n  $ lyra-cli media beats --input /tmp/clip.mp4 --output /tmp/beats.json --level 3\r\n  $ lyra-cli media beats --input /tmp/song.m4a --level-count 2\r\n  $ lyra-cli media beats --input /tmp/song.m4a --upload-vid v0123abcd\r\n\r\nNOTES\r\n  - Audio inputs (m4a/mp3/wav/...) are uploaded as-is.\r\n  - Video inputs are demuxed to a temporary m4a inside the runner; the\r\n    temporary file is removed when the request finishes.\r\n  - --upload-vid skips upload and uses an existing TOS vid.\r\n  - --level applies to the 5-gear API only (0=Level1Half, 1=Level1, ...).\r\n  - --output writes the full beats_json envelope to disk.\r\n",
